# This repository contains CODE ONLY. No data (raw, processed, patient-level or
# intermediate results) may be committed.
#
# Whitelist approach: ignore everything, then allow only code and documentation.
# If you add a new kind of code file (e.g. .py, .sh), add it to the list below.

*
!*/

# Code
!*.R
!*.Rmd
!*.py
!*.sh

# Documentation and environment
!README.md
!LICENSE
!LICENSE.md
!CITATION.cff
!.gitignore
!renv.lock
!*.Rproj

# renv infrastructure (so others can run renv::restore())
!.Rprofile
!renv/activate.R
!renv/settings.json

# Never commit data/result folders, even if they contain code-like files
**/Inputs/
**/Outputs/
**/WGS_input/
**/WGS_results/
**/meta/
**/data/

# R / OS clutter (already excluded by the whitelist; listed for clarity)
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.DS_Store

# Local helpers and verification results (not part of the repository)
run_all.R
compare_outputs.R
setup_renv_environment.R
verification_renv/
omnipathr-log/
**/omnipathr-log/
